---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="VPN"
    categorySlug="vpn"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">When Your Shows Disappear</h2>
  <p>
    Landed in Tokyo last fall after this miserable 14-hour flight. Finally get to the hotel. All I want is The Office
    and sleep. Open Netflix and it's... all Japanese. My show's gone. Everything's different.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nobody warns you about this.
  </p>
  <p>
    Portugal was the same thing. Three episodes into something good, fly to Lisbon, "not available in your region."
    Thanks for that.
  </p>
  <p>
    So here's what's happening. Netflix in America has completely different stuff than Netflix in England. Different
    shows, different movies. Disney+ releases things months apart depending on where you are. BBC iPlayer won't even
    load unless you're physically in the UK. Some licensing thing.
  </p>
  <p>
    VPN fixes it. You connect through an American server, Netflix sees an American IP, your shows come back. That's it.
    That's the whole trick.
  </p>
  <p>
    Spent a few months testing these things for streaming specifically. Which actually work? Which buffer constantly?
    Which survive garbage hotel WiFi?
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you're skimming:</strong> NordVPN. It's what I use. Works with everything. ExpressVPN for speed freaks.
    Surfshark if money's tight—two bucks and change monthly.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Picks Table -->
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={quickPicksColumns}
      rows={quickPicksRows}
      caption="Top 3 VPNs for streaming abroad"
  />

  <!-- Why Most VPNs Fail -->
  <h2 id="why-fail">Why Most VPNs Fail at This</h2>
  <p>
    Netflix hunts VPN connections and blocks them. So do the others. It's constant.
  </p>
  <p>
    The VPNs that work keep rotating their IP addresses to stay ahead. Cat and mouse. Costs money to maintain. Free VPNs
    don't bother, which is why they fail instantly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Speed matters too. Connecting is one thing. Buffering every 30 seconds makes it unwatchable. Need under 20%
    slowdown. Closer to 15% is better.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some nail Netflix but bomb on Disney+. Or BBC iPlayer. Tested all the big ones.
  </p>

  <!-- Top VPNs for Streaming -->
  <h2 id="top-vpns">These Actually Work</h2>

  <!-- NordVPN -->
  <h3 id="nordvpn">NordVPN</h3>
  <p>
    My daily driver for about a year.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honestly it just... works? Threw everything at it. Netflix US, UK, Japan, Australia. Disney+. Hulu. BBC iPlayer. HBO
    Max. Prime. Even Peacock which blocks most VPNs. First try, connected, loaded. SmartPlay does something in the
    background—don't ask me what—but streaming stuff loads noticeably faster.
  </p>
  <p>
    Things I noticed:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Tons of servers, always find one close</li>
    <li>NordLynx is quick</li>
    <li>Smart DNS for my old Roku that can't run apps</li>
    <li>10 devices covers everyone I travel with</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    11% speed hit. Watched 4K on crummy 50 Mbps hotel WiFi. Worked fine.
  </p>
  <p>
    Annoying part? $3.39/month sounds cheap but you're paying two years upfront. App's also cluttered with stuff I don't
    need.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/nordvpn"
      text="Get NordVPN — Best for Streaming"
      variant="primary"
      program="nordvpn"
  />

  <!-- ExpressVPN -->
  <h3 id="expressvpn">ExpressVPN</h3>
  <p>
    The fast one. Actually fast.
  </p>
  <p>
    8% slowdown. Best I measured. 4K worked on mediocre connections without issues.
  </p>
  <p>
    Haven't had a single connection refused. People complain about VPNs getting detected mid-show—hasn't happened once
    with this.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lightway protocol is genuinely quick. MediaStreamer for devices without app support. Their support chat actually
    knows things.
  </p>
  <p>
    Problem is $6.67/month for the annual plan. And 8 device limit which sounds fine until you count everything you own.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/expressvpn"
      text="Try ExpressVPN — Fastest Speeds"
      variant="primary"
      program="expressvpn"
  />

  <!-- Surfshark -->
  <h3 id="surfshark">Surfshark</h3>
  <p>
    Budget pick that actually works.
  </p>
  <p>
    $2.49 monthly. Unlimited devices. Everything you own, one subscription. Parents' iPad, roommate's laptop, whatever.
  </p>
  <p>
    Netflix worked. Disney+ worked. Hulu, BBC iPlayer, all fine. Sometimes a server gets blocked and you try another.
    Takes 30 seconds.
  </p>
  <p>
    15% slower. You notice if you look for it. Normal watching is fine.
  </p>
  <p>
    Support was slow when I needed them. Day and a half for a real response. Speeds jump around between servers.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/surfshark"
      text="Get Surfshark — Best Value"
      variant="primary"
      program="surfshark"
  />

  <!-- CyberGhost -->
  <h3 id="cyberghost">CyberGhost</h3>
  <p>
    Streaming for people who don't want to think.
  </p>
  <p>
    Servers labeled by service. Click "Netflix US." Click "BBC iPlayer." Done. No hunting for servers that work.
  </p>
  <p>
    11,000 servers. 45-day refund window. $2.19 monthly.
  </p>
  <p>
    18% slower but the streaming servers are faster than regular ones.
  </p>
  <p>
    Skip it for China or UAE. Interface looks dated.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/cyberghost"
      text="Get CyberGhost — 45-Day Trial"
      variant="secondary"
      program="cyberghost"
  />

  <!-- PIA -->
  <h3 id="pia">PIA</h3>
  <p>
    Ancient. Been around forever. 35,000 servers. Unlimited devices. $2.19 monthly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Netflix US, Disney+, Hulu, Prime—solid. HBO Max mostly worked. BBC iPlayer was spotty. Maybe 70% success.
  </p>
  <p>
    They've been subpoenaed and had nothing to hand over. Logs policy actually tested in court.
  </p>
  <p>
    17% slower.
  </p>
  <p>
    US company which bothers some people. BBC iPlayer issues would annoy me if I watched a lot of UK stuff.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/pia"
      text="Get PIA — Unlimited Devices"
      variant="secondary"
      program="pia"
  />

  <!-- IPVanish -->
  <h3 id="ipvanish">IPVanish</h3>
  <p>
    Mid-range. Unlimited devices.
  </p>
  <p>
    US content worked—Netflix, Hulu, Disney+. International was worse. Prime got blocked. BBC and HBO were inconsistent.
  </p>
  <p>
    $2.99 monthly. 20% slower.
  </p>
  <p>
    Works for American stuff. But same price gets you Surfshark or CyberGhost with better coverage.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/ipvanish"
      text="Get IPVanish"
      variant="ghost"
      program="ipvanish"
  />

  <!-- ProtonVPN -->
  <h3 id="protonvpn">ProtonVPN</h3>
  <p>
    Privacy crowd. You know who you are.
  </p>
  <p>
    Same people who make ProtonMail. Swiss. Open source. No ads. Strong privacy laws.
  </p>
  <p>
    Plus plan does everything—Netflix in 10+ countries, Disney+, Prime, BBC iPlayer, Hulu, HBO. Free tier doesn't
    stream.
  </p>
  <p>
    14% slower.
  </p>
  <p>
    $4.99 monthly is higher but you're paying for Swiss privacy.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/protonvpn"
      text="Get ProtonVPN Plus"
      variant="ghost"
      program="protonvpn"
  />

  <!-- Streaming Compatibility -->
  <h2 id="streaming-compatibility">Compatibility Summary</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Works with everything:</strong> NordVPN, ExpressVPN, Surfshark, CyberGhost, ProtonVPN
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Most things:</strong> PIA (BBC unreliable)
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>US stuff:</strong> IPVanish
  </p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={streamingColumns}
      rows={streamingRows}
      caption="VPN streaming platform compatibility"
  />

  <!-- Speed Tests -->
  <h2 id="speed-tests">Speeds I Measured</h2>
  <p>
    100 Mbps baseline to US, UK, Japan:
  </p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={speedColumns}
      rows={speedRows}
      caption="VPN speed test results for streaming"
  />
  <p>
    All handle HD. 4K wants ExpressVPN, NordVPN, or ProtonVPN.
  </p>

  <!-- Setup Guide -->
  <h2 id="setup-guide">Getting Started</h2>
  <p>
    Five minutes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subscribe to one. Download their app. Connect to whatever country has your content—US for American Netflix, UK for
    iPlayer. Open the streaming app. Should work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Doesn't work? Disconnect, try another server same country.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use WireGuard or NordLynx or Lightway for speed. Close other apps eating bandwidth.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <FAQSection faqs={faqs}/>

  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <h2 id="conclusion">My Take</h2>
  <p>
    Months of testing.
  </p>
  <p>
    NordVPN works. Fast enough. Unblocks everything. What I use.
  </p>
  <p>
    ExpressVPN fastest. Costs more.
  </p>
  <p>
    Surfshark cheapest that works. Unlimited devices.
  </p>
  <p>
    30-day refunds on all of them. Try one. If it doesn't work for your trips, try another.
  </p>
  <p>
    Next time you're stuck somewhere with blocked content you'll remember this. Just set it up.
  </p>

  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/nordvpn"
      text="Get NordVPN — Our #1 Pick for Streaming"
      variant="primary"
      program="nordvpn"
  />

  <!-- Related Articles -->
  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
